Some thoughts:

I'd like the ability to leave traces for other players to see. This could be
done by creating more effects similar to bone levels. One could
envision Oracles not only giving advice, but also asking for it. Peaceful creatures might sometimes #chat too (not just up-nosed manes). This could
be distributed to other- or later players by creatures (a nymph coming
with gossip-mail), or "mini-bones" with player messages that would pop up
later, for example by using walls to put messages on (won't rub out);

  Something is written on this wall, - more -
  "Gruc the Caveman loves nurses"

Since we don't have toilet wall's to write on, this might satisfy the 
literary exibitionists. Above all I just miss a little more of the unexpected 
*AND* humourous.


And to satisfy the truly curious, could a kind C-competent person compile a
program that can take a peak at or list from save- and bones-files? It 
shouldn't take too long given existing code. I took a look at some of the code 
and found out that my own knowledge of C is not adequate. But I did find some 
things that amused me, this one is from eat.c:

        if (pl_character[0] == 'K' && u.ualigntyp == U_LAWFUL)
                u.ualign--;     /* gluttony is unchivalrous */

So Knights; remember to think about your alignment when seeing that delicious
crisp fried strawberry-topped giant corpse.

Sincerely,
